WHAT IS INCLUDED
  prompts/*.py
      Verbatim copies of deepteam/attacks/single_turn/<attack>/template.py from the
      main branch (fetched 2026-08-28), unmodified:
        authority_escalation · emotional_manipulation · permission_escalation ·
        roleplay · prompt_probing

HOW IT IS USED (scenarios/attacks.py)
  Each template gives enhance(input) -> a prompt that rewrites a baseline attack into
  that framing, and is_<x>(response) -> a prompt that checks the rewrite still shows
  the framing. Both are applied as written, with DeepTeam's own discipline: up to
  three attempts, then the plain baseline rather than a rewrite that failed its check.
  The baseline is the red-team scenario text from scenarios/redteam.yaml.

NOT INCLUDED
  Obfuscation framings (base64, rot13, leetspeak, ...): no real user sends them.
  Multi-turn attacks: they refine against live replies and cannot be prepared offline.
